    supportWords: ['I would like to propose', 'compost', 'roster', 'approval', 'Yours sincerely'],
    requiredChecks: [{ id: 'p5-compost-problem', label: 'Explain the problem', keywordsAny: ['fruit peel', 'peel', 'waste', 'thrown away', 'throw away', 'throws away', 'rubbish', 'bins'] }, { id: 'p5-compost-plan', label: 'Explain how it would work and where the bin goes', keywordsAny: ['compost bin', 'garden', 'roster', 'take turns', 'each group', 'next to', 'beside'], minimumHits: 2 }, { id: 'p5-compost-ask', label: 'Ask for approval and one thing you need', keywordsAny: ['approval', 'approve', 'permission', 'may we', 'could you', 'we need', 'we would need', 'would you'] }],
    rubric: ['All three points covered with facts', 'Formal tone, greeting and sign-off', 'A subject line'],
    sampleAnswer: 'Subject: Proposal for a class composting project\n\nDear Mr Goh,\n\nI am writing on behalf of 5 Harmony to propose a composting project. After recess, our class throws away about two bags of fruit peel every week. This waste goes into the rubbish bins, even though it could be put to good use.\n\nWe would like to place a compost bin next to the school garden. Each group in our class would be on a roster for one week. The group on duty would collect the peel after recess, add dry leaves and turn the compost every Friday. After a few weeks, the compost could be used as fertiliser for the school garden.\n\nMay we have your approval to start next month? We would also need your help to order one compost bin through the Green Club.\n\nThank you for considering our proposal. We look forward to your reply.\n\nYours sincerely,\nNur Aisyah\nClass Representative, 5 Harmony',
